  "query_preview": "..\n\nA cold front will track through the region today with an upper\ntrough digging into the pacific northwest. This will place NE\nMontana under southwest flow aloft initially with increasing\nchances for rain ahead of the trough Saturday night with a\nshortwave ejecting out ahead of the closed low and plenty of\navailable moisture. \n\nThe low eventually cuts off as the shortwave gets absorbed in the\nnorthern stream over the Plains, resulting in a sort of split flow.\nThat northern system will eventually translate east toward the \nDakotas and Minnesota by Tuesday of next week. As this plays out \nlook for rain to continue at times through Monday. As temperatures\nfall, look for a mix with or change to wet snow Sunday into \nMonday. Ground temperatures are still warm so expect little if any\naccumulation of snow, but there could be a couple of inches over \nthe higher peaks of the Little Rockies. Meanwhile wetting rains \nwill be widespread, with NBM mean solution now around and \nexceeding 0.50\" QPF south of Highway 2 over the three day period.\n \nThe system takes the exit by Tuesday with a northern stream ride\nsetting up over the Northern High Plains while the closed low\ntracks south of the region. This low may track close enough to\nprovide light precipitation as far west as the Yellowstone\nCorridor within our CWA from Terry to Glendive Wednesday into\nThursday.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\nConfidence is increasing that the next system approaching on\nSaturday through Monday will bring beneficial amounts of\nprecipitation, though given warm ground temperatures and marginal\nthermal profiles, below average confidence exists on snow as a\nprecipitation type, timing of any changeover, or any accumulation,\nsave for the higher terrain such as the Little Rockies.\n\nConfidence is also below average on precipitation chances later in\nthe week as ensembles show increasing spread at larger time\nscales. It is possible the low tracks too far to the southeast for\nanything significant, other than increasing clouds and light\nprecipitation. Will be monitoring in the coming days for any\ntrends.",
